pstack
-------
The map is derived from pstack, a Cursor plugin by Lauren Tan.
pstack's content (skills, playbooks, principles, scripts, and references)
and its license are Lauren Tan's.

  Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan
  License: MIT
  Source: https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  License text: https://github.com/cursor/plugins/blob/main/pstack/LICENSE

data/graph.json is generated from that tree. It is not a copy of the
skill files; those stay in cursor/plugins. The live page links back to
the pinned commit.

Three.js
--------
vendor/ contains Three.js r169 (0.169.0), MIT license.

  Copyright 2010-2024 Three.js Authors
  https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js
  https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/r169/LICENSE

Vendored files, unchanged from three.js r169 except for the patch noted below:

  vendor/three.module.min.js
  vendor/CSS2DRenderer.js
  vendor/lines/Line2.js
  vendor/lines/LineGeometry.js
  vendor/lines/LineMaterial.js
  vendor/lines/LineSegments2.js
  vendor/lines/LineSegmentsGeometry.js

CSS2DRenderer.js includes a one-line pstack-map patch, marked in the source.
Upstream r169 writes fractional CSS pixel offsets. This copy wraps those
offsets in Math.round so labels sit on whole pixels:

  element.style.transform = 'translate(' + ( - 100 * object.center.x ) + '%,'
    + ( - 100 * object.center.y ) + '%)' + 'translate('
    + Math.round( _vector.x * _widthHalf + _widthHalf ) + 'px,'
    + Math.round( - _vector.y * _heightHalf + _heightHalf ) + 'px)';

Keep that Math.round if Three.js is upgraded.

